    "q-93743": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93743",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following pairs $(x,y)$ are solutions of the Diophantine equation $x+5y=85?$\n\nI. $(15,18)$\n\nII. $(10,15)$\n\nIII. $(5,16)$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's check each pair in turn.\n\n- $(15,18)$ is *not* a solution of our equation. Substituting $x=15$ and $y=18,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =85 \\\\ 15+5\\cdot 18 & =85 \\\\ 15+90 & =85 \\\\ 105 & \\ne 85\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(10,15)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=10$ and $y=15,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =85 \\\\ 10+5\\cdot 15 & =85 \\\\ 10+75 & =85 \\\\ 85 & =85\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(5,16)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=5$ and $y=16,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =85 \\\\ 5+5\\cdot 16 & =85 \\\\ 5+80 & =85 \\\\ 85 & =85\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
